// A list literal in a bytes slot is a bytes value, and the emitters ask
// type_of to say so. The literal has no parent link, so the question is asked
// backwards from the slots (a declaration, an assignment, a call or
// constructor argument): bytesmark holds a 1 for every literal some node hands
// a bytes type, built by one pass over the store the first time a literal asks.
// It is recomputed from the store alone, so a build that skips the type check
// (a front-end cache hit) answers the same as one that ran it.

